    "notes": "This view focuses on the Cdkn2a locus in Kras-engineered MCCA models. Samples are grouped by *CancerType*, groups with at least 10 samples are retained, and rows are sorted by the minimum copy-ratio value at Cdkn2a. This makes focal Cdkn2a-region losses stand out from broader chromosome 4 copy-number changes.\n\nThe strongest focal losses are visible in pancreatic cancer, with additional focal events in intestinal and lung cancer. This is consistent with the paper's conclusion that Cdkn2a inactivation is especially frequent in Kras-driven pancreatic cancer, while being less common but still present in lung and intestinal models. The paper links this pattern to tissue-specific Cdkn2a regulation: Cdkn2a is strongly induced during Kras-initiated early pancreatic oncogenesis, but increases only slightly during early intestinal tumour evolution.\n\nThe *Cdkn2a* and *Kras* transcriptome columns show expression z-scores for the same MCCA cell lines and can be used to inspect whether local copy-ratio changes coincide with expression changes. These values provide sample-level context, but they are not a direct reproduction of the paper's early-lesion or cell-of-origin expression analyses. The derived *Cdkn2a CN* column is a visual ranking score based on local log2 copy-ratio, not a curated deletion call."
  },
