    "notes": "This plot compares the derived *Cdkn2a CN* score with Cdkn2a expression in Kras-engineered MCCA models. *Cdkn2a CN* is the minimum log2 copy-ratio value over the Cdkn2a locus, while *Transcriptome/Cdkn2a* is the cell-line expression z-score from the MCCA transcriptome source.\n\nStrong local Cdkn2a-region copy losses form a clear left-side cluster and generally coincide with low Cdkn2a expression. Samples near neutral copy ratio show a much wider expression range, indicating that Cdkn2a expression varies beyond local copy number alone.\n\nThis supports reading the deep Cdkn2a-region losses as expression-associated events in these cell lines. The broader context from the paper is that Cdkn2a regulation is strongly tissue-specific. The plot is exploratory: *Cdkn2a CN* is a local copy-ratio ranking score, not a curated deletion call."
