    "notes": "This bookmark compares four related MCCA lines from mouse FKC076, corresponding to the FKC076 phylogeny shown in Fig. 5j of the MCCA paper. The view derives a *Kras CN* column from the brushed Kras locus on chromosome 6 and shows copy-ratio profiles across a broad genomic window.\n\nThe FKC076-derived lines share a common background, but FKC076_PTu-1 shows a clear whole-chromosome 6 gain, which includes Kras. This matches the Fig. 5j interpretation, where increased KrasG12D dosage is assigned to the P1 branch rather than shared by all FKC076-derived lines.\n\nThis is a visual comparison of related lines, not an independent cohort analysis. *Kras CN* is a local weighted-mean log2 copy-ratio score used to summarize the Kras locus, not the paper's full Kras allelic-state call, which also uses KrasG12D variant allele information."
